+permits local scripts, open a temporary session from this checkout with
+`powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned`, then continue below.
+`exit` closes that session; no persistent policy changes are needed. A process
+policy cannot override Group Policy. If it remains blocked, follow your
+organization's policy. See [PowerShell execution policies](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_execution_policies).
